<title>FRANCE: BIC acquires German pen manufacturer.</title>
<headline>BIC acquires German pen manufacturer.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pen and lighter manufacturer BIC said its German wholly-owned subsidiary BIC GmbH had acquired A. Hauser &amp; Co KG, based in Gosheim, and its subsidiaries for around 70 million francs, including the assumption of debt.</p>
<p>Hauser makes writing materials and specialises in felt pens.</p>
<p>BIC said in its nine-month sales statement that the acquisition closed on October 2.</p>
<p>&quot;This acquisition represents a further step in our strategy to increase the number of new products and reduce the gap between their conception and arrival to the market,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
